# Doc sync (crabmate-client)

## EN/ZH sync (hard rule)

- When bilingual pairs exist, **update both sides in the same change**; never English-only or Chinese-only
- Current pair: `README.md` ↔ `README.zh-CN.md`
- Facts, commands, paths, and constraints must match; wording may be localized; content drift is forbidden
- Future `*.zh-CN.md` / English counterparts follow the same rule
- `AGENTS.md` is **English-only** (no `AGENTS.zh-CN.md`)

## Update in this repo

- User-visible shell behavior → **`README.md` + `README.zh-CN.md` (must sync)**, plus matching `desktop-tauri/` / `mobile-tauri/` READMEs
- Agent / contributor constraints → **`AGENTS.md`** (English only)
- Connect model, lifecycle, tray / single-instance → `docs/design/tauri_gui_mvp_design.md`
- Coding-agent client plan (review / revert; not full IDE) → `docs/design/coding_agent_client.md` (Wave 1 checkboxes: `chat_ui_todo.md`; restore/changelog JSON: Server)
- Desktop / Android / Web / TUI capability cells → `docs/design/client_capability_matrix.md` (same PR as the capability change)
- Manual shell smoke steps → `docs/design/shell_smoke_runbook.md`
- Test / check entrypoints → `docs/TESTING.md`, `AGENTS.md` Required Commands
- User/maintainer release notes → `CHANGELOG.md` (English; `[Unreleased]`; move into a version section when tagging)

## Do not reinvent here

Write these in the **Server** repo; this repo only links:

- SSE / HTTP contracts, error codes, `request_id`
- CORS, `CM_WEB_*`, API base semantics
- `client-contract-v*` release policy
- Path A ADR / Phase todo checkboxes

## Forbidden

- Citing `agent_space/` drafts as authoritative docs
- Using a path dep back into the Server tree to “sync” Server docs in this PR
- Updating only one side of a bilingual pair
